lic anastomosis is a surgical procedure performed to connect the jejunum to the colon after resection of the ileum.", "YEYUNOSTOMÍA DE DESCARGA:The \"YEYUNOSTOMÍA DE DESCARGA\" refers to a jejunostomy procedure specifically designed for decompression. This surgical intervention involves creating an opening in the jejunum to alleviate intestinal obstruction or to manage excessive output from an ileostomy. While the procedure is essential for diverting intestinal contents due to the patient's medical condition, it also carries the risk of leading to nutritional deficiencies. Therefore, careful management of nutrition is crucial following the surgery to ensure the patient's health and well-being.", "SERVICIO DE CIRUGÍA GENERAL:The General Surgery Service is responsible for the surgical treatment of patients, including those with complex abdominal conditions.", "E. DE CROHN:E. de Crohn is an inflammatory bowel disease that causes inflammation of the digestive tract, leading to various complications.", "PERITONITIS FECALOIDEA:Fecaloid peritonitis is an inflammation of the peritoneum caused by the leakage of intestinal contents into the abdominal cavity, often requiring surgical intervention.", "DRENADO QUIRÚRGICO:Surgical drainage is a procedure performed to remove pus or fluid from an abscess, which was done for the patient’s abscess in the right flank.", "LAPARATOMÍA EXPLORADORA:Exploratory laparotomy is a surgical procedure to open the abdomen and examine the organs, which was performed on the patient to assess her condition.", "ANASTOMOSIS ILEOTRANSVERSA:Ileotransverse anastomosis is a surgical connection made between the ileum and the transverse colon, which was part of the patient’s surgical treatment.", "DÉBITO FECALOIDEO:Fecaloid output refers to the discharge of fecal matter from a surgical site, which the patient experienced post-surgery.", "FÍSTULA INTESTINAL:An intestinal fistula is an abnormal connection between the intestine and another organ or the skin, which the patient was suspected to have developed.", "DRENADO Y DESBRIDAMIENTO:Drainage and debridement are surgical procedures to remove infected tissue and fluid, which were performed on the patient during her treatment.", "DULAGLUTIDE:Dulaglutide es un medicamento utilizado para el tratamiento de la diabetes en la paciente.", "SIC:SIC, or síndrome de intestino corto, is a medical condition characterized by the preservation of less than 115 cm of small intestine. This condition can result in insufficient intestinal length, which may lead to the necessity for nutritional support to meet the patient's dietary needs.", "GRUPO ANDALUZ DE NUTRICIÓN E INVESTIGACIÓN:Este grupo ha publicado recomendaciones sobre el manejo de la glucemia en pacientes que inician nutrición artificial."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}